  "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer materials alternate HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand), starting with HfO2 at the air interface. Optimize all 24 individual layer thicknesses to maximize transmittance in 1530-1565nm band while maximizing reflectance in 400-700nm band. Use hybrid initialization: 60% of candidates start from quarter-wave optical thickness (center wavelength 550nm) with ±10% perturbation, 40% start from harmonic multiples (λ/8 and λ/2 optical thicknesses) with ±5nm random noise injection in the first optimization step. All thicknesses must remain between 40nm and 350nm. Total layer count is exactly 24. Materials are hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from the material catalog. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for each round.",
